.Dd September 3, 2026
.Dt CAPSULE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm capsule
.Nd capability-plane PID 1 init personality
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the
.Xr init 8
replacement that brings up the capability plane as process ID 1.
It is not a separate program: it is the PID-1
.Em personality
of
.Xr authorityd 8 ,
built from the same sources and installed as the boot copy
.Pa /sbin/capsule .
The daemon documentation, configuration, claims, and control interface are
described in
.Xr authorityd 8 ;
this page documents only the
.Nm
init role.
.Pp
The installed loader configuration
.Pq Pa /boot/loader.conf.d/capsule.conf
places
.Pa /sbin/capsule
first in
.Va init_path ,
with the stock
.Pa /sbin/init
and the rescue init as execution fallbacks, so the kernel execs
.Nm
as PID 1.
The copy lives in
.Pa /sbin
rather than
.Pa /usr
because
.Pa /usr
may be a separate filesystem that is not yet mounted when the kernel starts
init.
.Pp
When invoked as PID 1,
.Nm
does not daemonize and never exits: a PID-1 exit panics the kernel, so every
stock-init exit path becomes a logged emergency followed by a deliberate
.Xr reboot 2
or a drop to a recovery shell.
.Nm
runs a state machine ported from
.Xr init 8
with one additional state that brings up the
.Xr mac_capability 4
plane after
.Pa /etc/rc .
It performs the following duties:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Verifies that PID 1 already holds real-init reaper status, opens
.Pa /dev/mac_capability ,
and brings up the capability plane.
.It
Starts
.Xr serviced 8 ,
the capability service launcher, as its first managed child under a
process descriptor
.Pq Xr pdfork 2 .
.Nm
does not run
.Pa /etc/rc
itself;
.Xr serviced 8
owns rc startup and the native capability services, and
.Nm
waits for it to signal boot convergence before proceeding to multi-user.
If the plane or
.Xr serviced 8
cannot be brought up,
.Nm
enters a single-user recovery shell rather than a multi-user system with no
service world.
.It
Holds the signal shield across the whole boot window.
The
.Dv CP_SF_SIGNAL
capprotect flag is raised as soon as the
.Xr mac_capability 4
device is available, before
.Pa /etc/rc
runs, and re-asserted after convergence.
With the shield up, an ambient
.Xr kill 1
can never reach the legacy init transition handler; lifecycle transitions
arrive only over the capability plane.
.It
Acts as the system lifecycle, reboot, and halt authority.
Reboot, halt, power-off, power-cycle, single-user, and reroot requests are
delivered as an authorized
.Ql system.lifecycle
operation:
.Xr serviced 8
relays a request it authorized over its ADMIN-gated
.Ql system.lifecycle
capability to
.Nm ,
which applies it as a state-machine transition.
Command-line tools such as
.Xr reboot 8
and
.Xr shutdown 8
reach this path through
.Xr authorityctl 8 ,
falling back to
.Xr reboot 2 .
.El
.Pp
On a plane-free boot
.Pq loader tunable Va capability_plane Ns = Ns Qq NO ,
.Nm
hands PID 1 to the stock
.Pa /sbin/init
and the capability plane never starts; see
.Xr authorityd 8 .
In that mode
.Nm
holds no lifecycle authority.
.Ss Divergences from stock init
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Cm init Ar N
runlevel semantics
.Pq COMPAT_SYSV_INIT
are not accepted.
The stock
.Pa /sbin/init
remains installed for that use.
.It
.Va init_exec
is ignored: it is the hook that led the kernel to
.Nm ,
and honoring it again would exec-loop.
.It
Fatal errors and fatal signals reboot deliberately instead of exiting.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
is a boot program, not an interactive command; it takes no options beyond the
boot flags the kernel forwards to PID 1
.Pq for example Fl s No for single user .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /boot/loader.conf.d/capsule.conf" -compact
.It Pa /sbin/capsule
boot copy of the PID-1 program
.It Pa /boot/loader.conf.d/capsule.conf
loader configuration that selects
.Nm
as PID 1
.It Pa /dev/mac_capability
kernel capability device brought up at boot
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
.Xr reboot 2 ,
.Xr mac_capability 4 ,
.Xr authorityctl 8 ,
.Xr authorityd 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr serviced 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
personality appeared in
.Fx 5BSD
as the capability-plane replacement for
.Xr init 8 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
